# Client environment template — copy to .env and fill in real values.
# .env is gitignored; never commit your real .env.

# Google sign-in runs through Auth0 (SocialAuth uses connection=google-oauth2),
# so there is no VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID — the only client-side auth config is
# the Auth0 SPA application below. (Server-side GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID remains for
# the legacy direct /api/auth/google endpoint used by native clients/tests.)

# Auth0 — optional additive SSO (Universal Login). All three enable the
# "Continue with Auth0" button. Get them from Auth0 Dashboard > Application.
# VITE_AUTH0_DOMAIN=your-tenant.us.auth0.com
# VITE_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID=your_spa_client_id
# VITE_AUTH0_AUDIENCE= (optional API identifier, defaults to client ID)

# Split deploys — REQUIRED when the SPA is hosted apart from the API
# (e.g. Vercel frontend + persistent API host). The API + realtime host:
# VITE_API_URL=https://<your-api>/api
# VITE_SOCKET_URL=https://<your-api> (API origin, no /api)
# These are PUBLIC build-time values (baked into the bundle — never put
# secrets in VITE_*). Rebuild + redeploy the client after changing them.
#
# Single-origin deploys (API serves the built SPA itself) need neither:
# the app defaults to same-origin /api.
#
# Vercel project setup: Root Directory `client`, Framework Vite,
# Build `npm run build`, Output `dist` (see client/vercel.json + docs/ops/vercel.md).
# Preview deployments: same vars pointed at the staging API, with the preview
# origin added to the API's ALLOWED_ORIGINS.
